WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.114
Hi! Run, jump, eat, sleep: these are action words. Why is it sometimes run and sometimes runs? Let's find out.

2
00:00:12.264 --> 00:00:17.538
Action words tell us what someone does: run, jump, eat, read.

3
00:00:17.688 --> 00:00:22.122
For things we do every day or often, use the simple present.

4
00:00:22.272 --> 00:00:26.922
After I, you, we and they, the action word stays the same: We run.

5
00:00:27.072 --> 00:00:31.554
Every day is a clue for the simple present.

6
00:00:31.704 --> 00:00:36.786
After he, she or it, add s: He runs. She eats.

7
00:00:36.936 --> 00:00:40.674
One bird, so add s: The bird sings.

8
00:00:40.824 --> 00:00:44.706
Some words add es: goes, watches.

9
00:00:44.856 --> 00:00:48.738
They doesn't add s; it does.

10
00:00:48.888 --> 00:00:53.322
Watch out! The action word after Tom needs an s!

11
00:00:53.472 --> 00:00:56.202
Tom is one boy, so he.

12
00:00:56.352 --> 00:00:59.874
So it's Tom plays.

13
00:01:00.024 --> 00:01:07.698
Your turn! I, ___, to school. Pause and think.

14
00:01:07.848 --> 00:01:12.978
No s after I: walk. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:13.128 --> 00:01:21.042
Another one! She, ___, milk. Pause and think.

16
00:01:21.192 --> 00:01:26.658
Add s after she: drinks. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:26.808 --> 00:01:34.866
Here's another! The cat, ___, a lot. Pause and think.

18
00:01:35.016 --> 00:01:40.458
One cat is it: sleeps. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:40.608 --> 00:01:48.354
Try one more! We, ___, books. Pause and think.

20
00:01:48.504 --> 00:01:53.610
No s after we: read. Did you get it right?

21
00:01:53.760 --> 00:02:02.034
Try one more! He, ___, to bed at nine. Pause and think.

22
00:02:02.184 --> 00:02:07.626
After he, go becomes goes. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:07.776 --> 00:02:15.714
Try one more! Which is an action word? Pause and think.

24
00:02:15.864 --> 00:02:20.754
Jump is something you do. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:20.904 --> 00:02:28.818
Try one more! They, ___, in the park. Pause and think.

26
00:02:28.968 --> 00:02:34.122
No s after they: play. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:34.272 --> 00:02:42.690
Last one! Mum, ___, every morning. Pause and think.

28
00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:48.618
Mum is she, so add s: cooks. Did you get it right?

29
00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:55.817
Remember: use the simple present for everyday things. After he, she, it or one name, add s.

30
00:02:55.968 --> 00:03:01.385
Say what your family does every day: Dad cooks…

